<title>UK: BOC FY profit at top of analysts' forecasts.</title>
<headline>BOC FY profit at top of analysts' forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Sept 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		57.74		  vs 51.97</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 29.0		   vs 27.0</p>
<p> Pretax		     444.9		  vs 402.2</p>
<p> Turnover		   4.02 billion	 vs 3.75 billion</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts for pre-tax profits were in a range of 421 to 445 million stg. The dividend is declared in advance for the current financial year, to the end of September 1997.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 539.4		  vs 496.4</p>
<p> Exceptional		nil		    vs nil</p>
<p> Interest charge	  94.5		   vs 94.2</p>
<p> Tax			  137.9		  vs 128.6</p>
<p> Net taxed		  307.0		  vs 273.6</p>
<p> Retained		   278.3		  vs 249.0</p>
<p> Pay date (interim)     Feb 3, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  Dec 3</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Nov 25</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
